# ReMo Project Memory

Use ReMo to keep this repository's project memory current.

Canonical ReMo source: `skills/remo/SKILL.md`.

Project memory location:

- Process logs: `.remo/logs/`
- Project knowledge: `.remo/knowledge/`
- Knowledge index: `.remo/knowledge/index.md`

Memory language: Simplified Chinese.

Methodology:

- Route before read: read `.remo/knowledge/index.md` before broad codebase exploration.
- Distill before store: store stable project understanding, not raw transcripts or obvious code facts.
- Evidence before trust: connect important claims to files, commits, PRs, logs, or user decisions.
- Context ROI: write memory only when it will save more future context than it costs to read.
- SKR: keep every log and knowledge sentence high-signal.

If `.remo/knowledge/index.md` is missing, initialize ReMo before broad exploration:

- Create `.remo/logs/` and `.remo/knowledge/`.
- Create `index.md`, `project-overview.md`, `architecture.md`, `domain-model.md`, `workflows.md`, `decisions.md`, `conventions.md`, `faq.md`, and `glossary.md`.
- Fill safe facts from existing docs and top-level structure.
- If the project has a Git remote, inspect commit history and group important historical commits into retrospective logs and more accurate baseline knowledge. Do not create one log per commit.
- Mark unknown sections as `Status: To be filled` with concrete open questions.
- Add every baseline knowledge file to `index.md`.
- Create an installation log in Simplified Chinese.

Before broad codebase exploration:

- Read `.remo/knowledge/index.md` if it exists.
- Use the index to select the smallest relevant knowledge files.
- Scan code only when the knowledge base is missing, stale, contradicted, or not specific enough.

Before finishing meaningful work, do a ReMo check:

- Did this work create a milestone, decision, pivot, or important checkpoint? If yes, update `.remo/logs/`.
- Did this work produce stable project knowledge that should help future agents avoid rediscovery? If yes, update `.remo/knowledge/`.
- Did this work change or invalidate existing knowledge? If yes, update the relevant knowledge file.
- Did this work add, rename, or change the purpose of a knowledge file? If yes, update `.remo/knowledge/index.md`.
- Would the memory fail the Context ROI test? If yes, do not write it.

Commit and push checkpoint:

- Every commit and push must generate or update a ReMo log entry.
- Before committing, update affected `.remo/knowledge/` files and `.remo/knowledge/index.md` if the staged work changes durable project understanding.
- Include the ReMo updates in the same commit when they describe that commit's work.
- After pushing, update the log entry with commit hash, branch, remote, and push outcome when available.
- If no durable knowledge changed, state that in the log with the reason instead of inventing low-signal knowledge.

Use log paths like `.remo/logs/YYYY/MM/DD/HHMM-中文标题.md`. Store logs in year/month/day folders, keep the file timestamp numeric, and write the title segment in Simplified Chinese.

Keep log filenames, logs, and knowledge entries in Simplified Chinese, source-aware, and explicit about open questions.
